# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# SINGLE SOURCE OF TRUTH — every env var for the whole stack lives in
# this one file. Copy it to `.env` and fill in real values. There are
# NO per-profile `.env` files; compose maps these vars
# into each service as needed.
# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

# ── LLM Provider API Key (VPS-ONLY secret — never committed) ──────
# Real key lives ONLY in the git-ignored root `.env` on the VPS.
# Provider + model are picked per request in the Android app Settings
# (opencode | opencode-go) — one key covers both. This file carries placeholders only.
# OpenCode (direct, no LLM proxy); reaches only the pi service
OPENCODE_API_KEY=sk-...

# ── Skill test-fire model (bare direct-model calls, no persona/tools) ──
# Model id for taught-skill test fires (provider prefix optional).
# Scheduler fires do NOT use this: they run as chat-agent turns on the profile's
# running model, so they can read notes and fetch live pages at fire time.
# PI_TEACH_MODEL=mimo-v2.6-flash   # override (default: mimo-v2.6-flash)
# PI_CRON_MODEL is the retired name for the same setting, still honored as
# a fallback — existing deploys keep working.

# ── Android app password (single credential for chat + sync) ──────
# PASSWORD doubles as the app password: the pi-gateway
# chat API and health-api both accept it as the bearer credential, and the
# Android app sends it on every call (one Password field, no separate keys).
# Must match the Password field in Agento Settings.
# Generate with: openssl rand -hex 32
PASSWORD=change-me

# ── Single app URL (reverse proxy: chat + sync on one port) ─────────
# The proxy routes /p/* → pi :8643 (chat) and /api/* + /health →
# health-api :8000 (sync). Point the Agento app's Server URL here:
# http://<host>:8080 — one URL for chat AND sync. Direct ports
# (:8643, :8001) stay published for backward compatibility.
# APP_PORT=8080                   # override (compose default: 8080)
# PI_HOST_PORT=8643               # override (compose default: 8643)

# ── VPS SSH keys (retired side-profile git; host-side use only) ────────
# Read-only mounted into the pi service; only active when the dir holds
# id_ed25519(.pub) + known_hosts (missing files fail container creation).
# No profile clones or pulls on its own any more (#289).
# VPS_SSH_DIR=/root/.ssh          # override when the VPS user isn't root

# ── Remote MongoDB (Atlas: money/health/cookbook domain data) ───────
MONGODB_URI=mongodb+srv://user:pass@cluster0.example.mongodb.net/
MONGODB_DB=hermes

# ── Google connectors — OAuth + envelope key (#316) ────────────────
# POST /api/connectors/{id}/connect returns an auth_url the app opens in a
# browser; Google redirects to the single registered callback
# GET /api/connectors/callback?code=&state=, the server exchanges + stores
# encrypted tokens, and the connector flips to connected. Register this ONE
# redirect URI in the Google Cloud console (OAuth client, Web application).
# The path needs NO profile segment: the callback bypasses profile routing
# entirely, so register exactly:
#   http(s)://<host>:<port>/p/api/connectors/callback
# (through the proxy; direct: http://<host>:8643/api/connectors/callback).
# Any profile-prefixed spelling would also work (the segment is ignored),
# but register only this one — and never re-register on profile renames.
# Without all four values connect answers 501 and no token can be stored.
# The client must additionally carry Google's "AI-powered agent" flag
# (Cloud console → Google Auth Platform → Clients), or be a separate
# client created with that flag — without it the official MCP servers
# reject the vault's tokens. If the existing client serves non-agent
# features, mint a separate one and rotate all four values together.
# GOOGLE_CLIENT_ID=...            # OAuth client ID (not secret, but VPS-only)
# GOOGLE_CLIENT_SECRET=...         # OAuth client secret (VPS-ONLY secret — never committed)
# GOOGLE_REDIRECT_URL=...         # exact registered callback URL above
# Envelope key for OAuth tokens at rest (AES-256-GCM, server-side only).
# Generate with: openssl rand -hex 32. Missing = OAuth unconfigured.
# CONNECTORS_ENCRYPTION_KEY=...
